text:
The patient rain at early summer dawn;
The long, lone autumn drip; the damp, sweet


hush


Of springtime, when the glinting drops seem


gone
Into the first notes of the hidden thrush;


The solemn, dreary beat


OF winter rain and seet;
The mad glad, passionate calling of the showers


To the unblossomed hours;
The driving restless midnight sweep Of rain;
The ftful sobbing and the smile again
OF springs childhood; the fierce, IMPLYING pour
OF low-hung leaden clouds; the eyermore
Prophetic beauty of the sunset storm,
Transhgured into color and to form
Across the skye wondroHs changing ram!
Changeful and full OF temper as mans life;
Impetuous fierce. IMPLYING, kind again,
Prophetic, beauteous, soothing, full of strife;
Through all thy changing passions hear not We
Tn eternal note of the Unchanging Sea?


Laura Spencer Porror in the Atlantic.

